      "content": "Right, let's tackle this with the urgency of a horde of goblins on a treasure hunt. First, you need to find a safe, cool spot to park the truck. Think of it as finding a hidden cave where goblins can't reach. Once parked, check the temperature inside the truck. If it's above 40°F, you need to cool it down as quickly as possible. Use ice packs, frozen water bottles, or any other cooling resources you have. It's like trying to keep your precious goblin gold from melting in the sun.\n\nNow, for the food safety protocols, you need to ensure that the tuna is kept at a safe temperature. If the temperature has been above 40°F for more than 2 hours, it's time to consider the tuna as spoiled. But if it's been less than 2 hours, you can still salvage it by cooling it down to 40°F or below within 2 hours. Remember, it's like trying to keep your goblin snacks fresh for the next raid.\n\nOnce the truck is cooled down, check the tuna for any signs of spoilage. If it's still good, you can continue your journey. If not, you'll need to dispose of it properly to avoid any food safety issues. Think",
